  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 2.5199999809265137,
      "text": "Begin with the bean type external view.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 3.3399999141693115,
      "end": 4.980000019073486,
      "text": "A points to the protective seed coat.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 5.71999979019165,
      "end": 9.960000038146973,
      "text": "B identifies the hilum, the scar left by the former attachment to the funicle.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 10.65999984741211,
      "end": 15.602307869837833,
      "text": "C marks the smaller micropyle near it, a persistent opening associated with",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 15.602307869837833,
      "end": 15.800000190734863,
      "text": "the",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 15.800000190734863,
      "end": 16.559999465942383,
      "text": "ovule integuments.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 17.1200008392334,
      "end": 19.3799991607666,
      "text": "A scar is not the same as a pore.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 20,
      "end": 24.34000015258789,
      "text": "The seed coat commonly has an outer testa and an inner tegmen, but this",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 24.34000015258789,
      "end": 27.34000015258789,
      "text": "external outline does not resolve those layers separately.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 28.139999389648438,
      "end": 30.81999969482422,
      "text": "Seed shape and coat details vary among plants.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 31.559999465942383,
      "end": 35.779998779296875,
      "text": "Do not infer the exact internal axis position or the presence of mature",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 35.779998779296875,
      "end": 38.5,
      "text": "endosperm from this selected surface drawing alone.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 38.71200000000058,
      "end": 41.77199994278012,
      "text": "Add internal context without inventing a section.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 42.471999990463836,
      "end": 46.251999961853606,
      "text": "In familiar mature bean type seeds, much of the reserve food is in the",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 46.251999961853606,
      "end": 49.43200026702939,
      "text": "cotyledons and the endosperm has been used during development.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 50.05200015258847,
      "end": 55.05200015258847,
      "text": "This does not mean every dicot seed lacks retained endosperm; castor is a",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 55.05200015258847,
      "end": 56.61199961853085,
      "text": "familiar endospermous dicot example.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 57.33200083923398,
      "end": 60.91200076294003,
      "text": "Endosperm originates through the fertilisation pathway involving the central",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 60.91200076294003,
      "end": 64.01199923706113,
      "text": "cell, whereas persistent nucellus is called perisperm.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 64.01199923706113,
      "end": 68.85199938964902,
      "text": "Both terms concern tissue identity and developmental origin, not just where",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 68.85199938964902,
      "end": 69.47200022888242,
      "text": "food is stored.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 70.07200061035215,
      "end": 72.65199862670957,
      "text": "The embryo and seed coat also have different origins.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 73.31199847412168,
      "end": 77.67199908447324,
      "text": "A seed diagram should be read using its example and maturity stage rather than",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 77.67199908447324,
      "end": 80.5319996948248,
      "text": "a universal dicot versus monocot food storage rule.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 80.76000000000128,
      "end": 84.03999997139105,
      "text": "The second board spreads out a selected dicot embryo.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 84.83999992370734,
      "end": 88.62000013351569,
      "text": "A marks the cotyledons, with a corresponding cotyledon on the opposite side.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 89.19999958038458,
      "end": 92.1400001144422,
      "text": "B points to the plumule, the embryonic shoot region.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 92.82000041961798,
      "end": 97.0799996948255,
      "text": "C identifies the epicotyl, the portion of the embryonal axis above the",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 97.0799996948255,
      "end": 98.13999916076789,
      "text": "cotyledon attachment level.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 98.80000091552863,
      "end": 103.10666579809073,
      "text": "The horizontal dashed line is a reference for that level, not an extra organ",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 103.10666579809073,
      "end": 103.21999908447394,
      "text": "or",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 103.21999908447394,
      "end": 104.15999961853156,
      "text": "a cut through a vessel.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 105.02000022888312,
      "end": 108.86000038147101,
      "text": "Cotyledons are part of the embryo, not the seed coat and not endosperm.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 109.31999946594367,
      "end": 111.68000007629523,
      "text": "Their size and function vary among species.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 112.4199998474134,
      "end": 116.84000183105597,
      "text": "This simplified spread view exposes relationships that an intact external seed",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 116.84000183105597,
      "end": 117.84000183105597,
      "text": "drawing cannot show.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 118.0800000000018,
      "end": 122.02000005722226,
      "text": "D marks the hypocotyl, below the cotyledon attachment level.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 123.04000003814878,
      "end": 126.73999984741391,
      "text": "E points to the terminal radicle, the embryonic root region.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 127.6400004196185,
      "end": 132.68000038147153,
      "text": "Do not call the entire lower axis a radicle or confuse the hypocotyl with the",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 132.68000038147153,
      "end": 134.3600006866473,
      "text": "epicotyl above the attachment level.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 135.37999923706235,
      "end": 139.7999993133563,
      "text": "During ordinary germination the radicle develops into the primary root, while",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 139.7999993133563,
      "end": 141.44000061035337,
      "text": "the plumule contributes to the shoot.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 141.76000030517758,
      "end": 146.76000030517758,
      "text": "The drawing shows a selected embryo before seedling emergence, not the full",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 146.76000030517758,
      "end": 149.15999992370786,
      "text": "sequence of epigeal or hypogeal germination.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 150.05999954223813,
      "end": 153.6799984741229,
      "text": "A root emerging first does not prove that every seed follows an identical",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 153.6799984741229,
      "end": 154.28000076294126,
      "text": "timetable.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 155.26000030517758,
      "end": 158.9200001525897,
      "text": "Use positions relative to the cotyledonary node to interpret the labels.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 159.14400000000248,
      "end": 165.10400003814945,
      "text": "The maize longitudinal section is a grain, or caryopsis: a one seeded",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 165.10400003814945,
      "end": 168.06400007629642,
      "text": "fruit with its pericarp closely fused to the seed coat.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 169.1239995422388,
      "end": 171.26399988556156,
      "text": "A marks that combined outer region.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 172.1839999618555,
      "end": 176.82400030517826,
      "text": "B locates the peripheral aleurone region of the retained endosperm, while C",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 176.82400030517826,
      "end": 179.16400045776615,
      "text": "marks the large starchy endosperm region.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 179.16400045776615,
      "end": 182.52399916076908,
      "text": "Aleurone is not an extra maternal seed coat.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 183.14400000000248,
      "end": 187.00400061035404,
      "text": "The outlines locate tissue regions and do not resolve every cell layer.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 187.50400061035404,
      "end": 192.00400061035404,
      "text": "This grain retains substantial endosperm at maturity, unlike the familiar bean",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 192.00400061035404,
      "end": 193.40399832153568,
      "text": "type example discussed earlier.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 194.04400152588138,
      "end": 198.22400183105717,
      "text": "The comparison concerns the selected examples, not a rule that every monocot",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 198.22400183105717,
      "end": 199.94399923706303,
      "text": "must have an identical reserve pattern.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 200.20800000000315,
      "end": 204.86799984741526,
      "text": "D identifies the shield like scutellum on the embryo side of the maize grain.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 205.50800019073802,
      "end": 209.48799973297434,
      "text": "It is the single cotyledon of the grass embryo, not a separate piece of",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 209.48799973297434,
      "end": 209.8480003433259,
      "text": "endosperm.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 210.94799977112132,
      "end": 213.92800026703196,
      "text": "E locates the simplified embryonal axis.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 215.00800019073802,
      "end": 217.86799984741526,
      "text": "Together, scutellum and axis belong to the embryo.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 218.14800053406077,
      "end": 222.44799977112132,
      "text": "The scutellum assists transfer of reserves from endosperm during germination,",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 223.08799916076975,
      "end": 225.52799969482737,
      "text": "but that role does not change its embryonic identity.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 226.19799977112132,
      "end": 230.8479993896516,
      "text": "The large starchy region at C is endosperm rather than a giant",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 230.8479993896516,
      "end": 232.7480009155305,
      "text": "cotyledon.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 232.7480009155305,
      "end": 237.0079992370637,
      "text": "Position, developmental origin and connection with the axis are stronger clues",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 237.0079992370637,
      "end": 238.30799847412425,
      "text": "than relative size alone.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 239.22800045776683,
      "end": 242.4080007629426,
      "text": "The next board enlarges the axis and protective sheaths.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 242.61600000000388,
      "end": 248.5160000953713,
      "text": "The enlarged grass embryo labels A as scutellum, B as coleoptile and C as",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 248.5160000953713,
      "end": 248.75599986648947,
      "text": "plumule.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 249.35599977112204,
      "end": 253.34292306225504,
      "text": "The coleoptile is the protective sheath enclosing the young shoot region,",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 253.34292306225504,
      "end": 253.61600000000388,
      "text": "while",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 253.61600000000388,
      "end": 255.73599988556296,
      "text": "the plumule is the developing shoot within it.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 256.315999809269,
      "end": 258.6360004577675,
      "text": "They are not alternative names for the same structure.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 259.5360000762978,
      "end": 263.2160003814736,
      "text": "A visible enclosing outline should therefore be traced separately from the",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 263.2160003814736,
      "end": 263.855999771122,
      "text": "structure it protects.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 264.45600015259174,
      "end": 268.95600015259174,
      "text": "The scutellum remains the single cotyledon; neither protective sheath adds",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 268.95600015259174,
      "end": 269.83599931335834,
      "text": "another cotyledon.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 270.5360000762978,
      "end": 274.69138389548664,
      "text": "Endosperm and the outer grain coverings are omitted in this enlargement so",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 274.69138389548664,
      "end": 274.9159992370644,
      "text": "that",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 274.9159992370644,
      "end": 276.3959987793007,
      "text": "the axis can be read clearly.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 277.3160007629433,
      "end": 280.1560009155312,
      "text": "Do not identify the enlargement as an intact maize grain.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 280.36800000000443,
      "end": 285.90799996185746,
      "text": "D identifies the radicle and E the surrounding coleorhiza at the lower end of",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 285.90799996185746,
      "end": 286.8280000381514,
      "text": "the grass embryo.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 286.8280000381514,
      "end": 291.5480003051802,
      "text": "Coleorhiza protects the root region; coleoptile protects the shoot region",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 291.5480003051802,
      "end": 291.9280004196211,
      "text": "above.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 292.9280004196211,
      "end": 296.64800068664994,
      "text": "Pair each sheath with the structure inside it rather than memorising two",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 296.64800068664994,
      "end": 298.5480003051802,
      "text": "similar sounding names without positions.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 299.4279994659468,
      "end": 303.74799916077103,
      "text": "The axis links shoot and root regions, and the scutellum attaches laterally.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 304.4880008392378,
      "end": 309.24799916077103,
      "text": "This is a selected anatomical model, not a timed germination experiment or",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 309.24799916077103,
      "end": 312.68799969482865,
      "text": "evidence that every monocot embryo has exactly the same proportions.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 314.4080009155318,
      "end": 318.7341524454797,
      "text": "Finish by distinguishing coverings, reserve tissue, cotyledons and growing",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 318.7341524454797,
      "end": 318.9679984741255,
      "text": "axis",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 318.9679984741255,
      "end": 319.3880004577681,
      "text": "regions.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 320.18799969482865,
      "end": 323.5480003051802,
      "text": "Those categories prevent many common errors in seed label questions.",
      "chapter": 7
    }
  ]
}
